+| `Rule30LinearCharts` | 2026-11-11 | Every linear chart of the constrained zero-boundary starts is the free-bit chart. On `KK L := L 0 = false ∧ InX L`, `Theta` and the free-bit read-off `fb` are inverse bijections with all sequences that turn two steps into the one-sided shift (`kk_Theta`, `fb_Theta`, `Theta_fb`, `kk_two_step`, `fb_shift`, `uld_Theta`, `uld_fb`). If `A` is closed under `a + b + c` (pointwise xor), `Lm` is affine on `A`, and `Φ`, `Φ'` are mutually inverse between `KK` and `A`, uniformly finitely dependent, with `Φ (zrow L 2) = Lm (Φ L)`, then `Φ ∘ Theta` is affine (`linear_chart_is_free_bit_chart`, `free_bit_chart_affine`, `free_bit_chart_iso`; `free_bit_chart_is_chart` checks the free-bit chart itself). The proof is the group-law lemma `groupLaw_eq_xor`: a commutative operation on one-sided sequences with the white sequence as neutral element, `(x + y) + y = x`, commuting with the shift and with bit 0 fixed by a finite window, is pointwise xor (`fibre_form`, `involution_Q`, `flip_invariant`, `descent_step`, `window_zero`, `q_white`). Continuity is represented as uniform finite dependence; its equivalence with continuity on compact domains is not formalized. The automorphism theorem of the one-sided full 2-shift is due to Hedlund (1969); the lemma is probably known. Nothing here decides `Q01` or period 2. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI), as Rule 30 Prize submission [PORTAL-ID](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/PORTAL-ID). | `groupLaw_eq_xor`, `fibre_form`, `involution_Q`, `flip_invariant`, `descent_step`, `window_zero`, `q_white`, `kk_Theta`, `fb_Theta`, `Theta_fb`, `kk_two_step`, `fb_shift`, `uld_Theta`, `uld_fb`, `linear_chart_is_free_bit_chart`, `free_bit_chart_affine`, `free_bit_chart_iso`, `free_bit_chart_is_chart` |
